---
import { StepCode } from '../components/viz';
import src from '../../../sum.s?raw';

// the file minus its header comment (what you'd type live)
const code = src.slice(src.indexOf('    .data'));
---
<h2>our program: add up 8 numbers</h2>
<div class="prog">
  <StepCode client:load lang="asm" code={code} class="prog-code"
    hl={{ 1: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 2: [6, 7, 8], 3: [9, 10, 11], 4: [12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17], 5: [19, 20, 21], 6: [23, 24, 25] }} />
  <ol class="prog-steps">
    <li class="step"><b>.data</b>: the numbers, in memory. a label names each address</li>
    <li class="step"><b>.text</b>: the instructions. the cpu starts at <code>_start</code></li>
    <li class="step">t0 = where we are in the array, t1 = how many are left, t2 = the sum</li>
    <li class="step">the loop: load a number, add it, move to the next, count down, go again</li>
    <li class="step">store the sum in total. ebreak shows us the registers</li>
    <li class="step">ask the os to exit, with the sum as the exit code: a7 = 93 (exit), then <b>ecall</b></li>
  </ol>
</div>
<style>
  .prog { display: flex; gap: 2em; align-items: flex-start; }
  .prog :global(.prog-code) { flex: 1.25; }
  .prog :global(.prog-code pre) { font-size: .5em; margin: 0; }
  .prog-steps { flex: 1; font-size: .62em; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .prog-steps li { margin: .2em 0 .7em; }
</style>
